 **CL-013: Information-theoretic necessity condition.**  
 Status: promising direction.  
 A lower bound should use two processes/classes with identical observations before delayed feedback resolves, but different best fixed quotes. Long tail mass must be payoff-relevant, sufficiently frequent, and unpredictable.
+
+**CL-016: Concatenated block universal lower bound.**  
+Status: promising but not fully formalized.  
+Let \(N_i\) be dominant block lengths with \(M_i=\sum_{j<i}(N_j+1)=o(N_i)\), and consider deterministic sequences formed by blocks \(0^{N_i}c_i\), \(c_i\in\{1/2,1\}\). For any process-unaware universal learner, one should be able to choose \(c_i\)'s so that at block endpoints \(T_i=M_i+N_i+1\),
+\[
+R^\pi(T_i)\ge N_i/4-M_i,
+\]
+and hence \(\limsup_i R^\pi(T_i)/T_i\ge1/4\). Remaining work: state whether learners are horizon-aware or anytime, diagonalize if needed, condition on the fixed prior prefix for randomized learners, and write the cross-block pending-reward accounting carefully.
