working_notes/counterexamples.md:62:Choose an \(\varepsilon_T\)-optimizer of \(\sup_a V_T^P(a)\) and post it in every round. The learner's expected reward equals \(V_T^P(a_T)\), so its pseudo-regret is at most \(\varepsilon_T=o(T)\), regardless of \(\beta,\gamma,\Delta_T,\Gamma_T\), or any other tail statistic. This is not an algorithmic result unless the process law and horizon are known and approximate optimization is allowed.
